twice and had a couple yummy daiquiris that came with a souvenir cup. Tried the piña colada and also mixed strawberry with banana. Both were delicious, and helped beat the hot and humid 90+ degree NOLA weather! Also tried the hot wings and these were ok too. It's a nice place to go and have a quick bite to eat and a drink. Only thing I didn't like seeing was a guy with his dog inside. But other than that, I would def go again."},{"business_id":"v00u4Ui7dnHba1CrU_g40g","review_id":"thgaQNUuj4zP3xxCkbVEbw","date":"2011-08-17T14:21:33","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9019873142242432,"text_excerpt":"On a recent Saturday night, my husband and I wanted comically large libations in ridiculous containers, but wanted to be away from the fracas of Bourbon Street. With Big Easy Daiquiri's Canal Street location only a few blocks from our hotel, this was an easy task. My husband got the Jungle Juice and I got a Hurricane, both in the silly jumbo plastic fleur de lis glasses. Both were frosty, sweet and delicious - an excellent way to combat the heat and humidity on an August NOLA night. Being in New Orleans, we took our treats to the streets for a little shopping and strolling into the night. Unfortunately I noticed my glass started leaking a few blocks away from Big Easy. We went back and th..."},{"business_id":"v00u4Ui7dnHba1CrU_g40g","review_id":"ZRzn7niSdbf8Sf4uyu79Rw","date":"2011-04-29T03:35:00","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9003728032112122,"text_excerpt":"Needed some quick drinks because our hotel bar wasn't open yet. Bloody Mary's were very good as were their frozen drinks. Great choice on a hot humid NOLA morning."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"v00u4Ui7dnHba1CrU_g40g","photo_id":"r-Cq5xVHxtgK8V9F8IU2Qw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/r-Cq5xVHxtgK8V9F8IU2Qw.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
